The point: a shared record helped new agents recover a convention after their predecessors disappeared. But exposing the signals also helped an unintended observer learn that convention.

Those results come from a small, deliberately simplified model with rule-based learners—not autonomous frontier AI. They demonstrate the mechanism under those assumptions, not a scientific breakthrough.

The next serious test would be whether independently initialized, capable agents can accomplish this without receiving the same built-in learning procedure.

That could become an interesting public demonstration if it withstands independent replication and harder controls.

